WEBVTT

00:11:28.142 --> 00:11:32.648
and it's not their problem
if they see you a certain way.

00:11:32.672 --> 00:11:34.066
It's your problem."

00:11:34.090 --> 00:11:37.256
AG: Her therapist wasn't
advising her to be fake,

00:11:37.280 --> 00:11:40.056
but to avoid being
completely individualistic,

00:11:40.080 --> 00:11:42.394
to think of others, too.

00:11:42.418 --> 00:11:46.256
LF: I think that has benefited my life.

00:11:46.280 --> 00:11:49.670
AG: Sometimes people get so absorbed
in expressing their own opinions

00:11:49.694 --> 00:11:51.928
that they lose sight of
how they affect others.

00:11:52.410 --> 00:11:55.851
In Leah's view,
focusing less on authenticity

00:11:55.875 --> 00:11:57.801
has made her more effective.

00:11:58.240 --> 00:12:00.476
LF: I think I've become a lot more ...